
🏦 Banking System – Python Winter Sprint 2026

A simple CLI-based Banking System built using Python, focusing on functions, recursion, and file handling.
This project is part of Python Winter Sprint 2026 (Foundation Track) by Coding Council.

📌 Problem Overview

This program simulates a basic banking system where a user can:

Create a bank account

Deposit money

Withdraw money

Exit and view final account details

All account data is stored using file handling, and the menu runs using recursion instead of loops.

🧠 Concepts Used

Python Functions

Recursion

File Handling (read / write)

Basic Input & Output

Simple Logic (Beginner Friendly)

📂 Files Used

bank.txt → Stores account holder name and balance

⚙️ How the Program Works

Program starts

User enters:

Account holder name

Initial balance

Details are saved to bank.txt

Recursive menu appears:

Deposit money

Withdraw money

Exit

After exit:

File is read

Final account summary is displayed




📚 Learning Outcome

Understand how recursion can replace loops

Learn basic file-based data storage

Build confidence in writing real-world Python programs
